tp://www.cdma-acfpp.org/en/issues/noc_regulations.html"/><comment>accessed 15 January, 2006</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Office of Patented Medicines and Liaison</collab></person-group><article-title>Therapeutic Products Directorate statistical report 2004: patented medicines (notice of compliance) regulations</article-title><source>Health Canada</source><year>2005</year></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Office of Patented Medicines and Liaison</collab></person-group><article-title>Therapeutic Products Directorate statistical report 2004: patented medicines (notice of compliance) regulations</article-title><source>Health Canada</source><year>2005</year></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Rx&#x00026;D</collab></person-group><article-title>S-17: a necessary first step to bring Canada's patent act to internationally competitive standards. A brief to the House of Commons Standing Committee on Industry, Science and Technology</article-title><source>Ottawa</source><comment>May 29, 2001</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="other"><source>Government of Canada Canada Gazette Part II Regulations amending the patented medicines (notice of compliance) regulations</source><year>2006</year><volume>140</volume><fpage>1503</fpage><lpage>1525</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="other"><source>Canadian Generic Pharmaceutical Association Supreme Court decision proves Fed's gift to big pharma unnecessary</source><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.canadiangenerics.ca/en/news/nov_03_06.shtml"/><comment>accessed 10 December 2006</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Avorn</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Torcetrapib and Atorvastatin &#x02013; Should Marketing Drive the Research Agenda?</article-title><source>New England Journal of Medicine</source><year>2005</year><volume>352</volume><fpage>2573</fpage><lpage>2576</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15972861</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1056/NEJMp058075</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>US Food and Drug Administration</collab></person-group><article-title>Pfizer Stops All Torcetrapib Clinical Trials in Interest of Patient Safety</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.fda.gov/bbs/topics/NEWS/2006/NEW01514.html"/><comment>accessed 7 May 2007</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Burdon</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Sloper</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The Art of Using Secondary Patents to Improve Protection</article-title><source>International Journal of Medical Marketing</source><year>2003</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>226</fpage><lpage>229</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1057/palgrave.jmm.5040125</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="other"><source>Aktiebolaget Hassle v Alphapharm Pty Ltd, 212 CLR 411</source><year>2002</year></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="other"><source>Aktiebolaget Hassle v Alphapharm Pty Ltd, 212 CLR 411, para 101</source><year>2002</year></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="other"><source>Arrow Pharmaceuticals Limited v Merck &#x00026; Co, Inc, FCA 1282; 63 IPR 85</source><year>2004</year></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="other"><source>Arrow Pharmaceuticals Limited v Merck &#x00026; Co, Inc, FCA 1282 at para 80</source><year>2004</year></citation></ref><ref i